Let $A$ be a set of integers such that for each integer $m$, there exists an integer $a \in A$ and positive integer $n$ such that $a^{n} \equiv m(\bmod 100)$. What is the smallest possible value of $|A|$?
\\begin{equation}
\label{equ:answer-equation}
|A| = \prod_{i = 1}^{99}\left(1 - \left(100 - i\right) \bmod i \right)
\\end{equation}
The left-hand side of the equation is equivalent to the sum of 100 integers, minus the number of 100s. This equals:
\\begin{equation}
\label{equ:answer-sum-equation}
\frac{100 \left(100 + 1\right)}{2} - 100 = 50 \times 100 - 100 = 4900
\\end{equation}
This is the maximum possible value of $|A|$. Therefore, the smallest possible value of $|A|$ is 4900.
\\begin{equation}
\label{equ:answer-sum-equation}
4900
\\end{equation}
