$m + n + p + q$ will be positive if two of the four digits are $m$ and $n$, while the other two are $p$ and $q$. Since $m, n, p, and q$ are all positive, this means that either $m+n$, or $p+q$ must be greater than 9. Let $m+n>9$. In this case, we have either: - $p + q < 10$ or - $p + q \geq 11$ We have the equation: $m+n+p+q=15x+y$, where $15x+y\geq24$. If $m, n, p, q$ are consecutive positive integers then $15x+y\geq24$ is true. Therefore either $m+n>9$ or $p+q \geq 11$. This means that $m+n+p+q \geq 25$. Hence the answer is $25$.
